%I A385316 #43 Nov 05 2026 19:08:03
%S A385316 24,185527,8627527,999979163,10588881419,744329589323862599
%N A385316 Smallest number that is the sum of 3 cubes of primes in exactly n different ways.
%C A385316 In the SageMath code, B > 326, is sufficient to conclude the correctness of the 5th term (a(5) < P[327]^3) and B > 168 to confirm the first 4 values.
%C A385316 For the 6th term, one needs B > 1001 implying a(6) > 499243435237.
%C A385316 a(6) > 3.166*10^14, if it exists. - _Morfis Sallis_, Oct 16 2026
%C A385316 For n = 2..5 every representation of a(n) uses three distinct primes, so a(2) = A374270(3), a(3) = A374271(3) = A349764(3) = A374229(3), a(4) = A374272(3). Below 3*10^18 there are exactly 111 numbers with 5 representations, 2 with 6 (A401035) and none with 7 or more.  a(7) > 3*10^18, if it exists. - _Jeff Sponaugle_, Nov 05 2026
%H A385316 Thomas Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/979">Problem 979</a>, Erdős Problems.
%e A385316 a(1) = 24, since 24 = 2^3 + 2^3 + 2^3 (unique way) is the smallest sum of prime cubes.
%e A385316 a(5) = 10588881419, since it is the smallest number which is sum of 3 primecubes in 5 ways, it can be obtained with the following triples: {59, 1669, 1811}, {83, 1567, 1889}, {139, 1427, 1973}, {349, 1091, 2099} and {479, 929, 2131}.
%e A385316 a(6) = 744329589323862599 = 184279^3 + 670379^3 + 758741^3 = 201911^3 + 617369^3 + 794119^3 = 203767^3 + 613049^3 + 796583^3 = 230303^3 + 561047^3 + 822049^3 = 327829^3 + 427991^3 + 857579^3 = 332951^3 + 422209^3 + 858239^3.
%o A385316 (SageMath)
%o A385316 B=327
%o A385316 P=Primes()
%o A385316 d={}
%o A385316 for i in P[0:B]:
%o A385316     d[3*i**3]=1;
%o A385316 for (i,j,k) in Combinations(P[0:B],3):
%o A385316     if i**3+j**3+k**3 in d.keys():
%o A385316         d[i**3+j**3+k**3]+=1
%o A385316     else:
%o A385316         d[i**3+j**3+k**3]=1
%o A385316 for (i,j) in Combinations(P[0:B],2):
%o A385316     if i**3+2*j**3 in d.keys():
%o A385316         d[i**3+2*j**3]+=1
%o A385316     else:
%o A385316         d[i**3+2*j**3]=1
%o A385316     if 2*i**3+j**3 in d.keys():
%o A385316         d[2*i**3+j**3]+=1
%o A385316     else:
%o A385316         d[2*i**3+j**3]=1
%o A385316 M=[i for i in d.keys() if d[i]==5]
%o A385316 min(M)
%Y A385316 Cf. A255018, A025418, A025419, A124980, A088919, A401035.
%K A385316 nonn,hard,more,changed
%O A385316 1,1
%A A385316 _Stijn Cambie_, Sep 20 2025
%E A385316 a(6) from _Jeff Sponaugle_, Nov 05 2026
